message: "If you use AgentKillChain in academic, policy, or safety evaluation work, please cite it using this metadata."
title: "AgentKillChain: A Controlled Benchmark for Persistent Compromise in Autonomous AI Agents"
authors:
  - family-names: "O'Connor"
    given-names: "Kevin"
repository-code: "https://github.com/KevinOBytes/AgentKillChain"
url: "https://github.com/KevinOBytes/AgentKillChain"
license: "MIT"
date-released: "2026-05-20"
version: "1.1.0"
keywords:
  - "AI safety"
  - "agent evaluation"
  - "prompt injection"
  - "memory poisoning"
  - "tool use"
  - "frontier model evaluation"
abstract: >-
  AgentKillChain is an open, controlled benchmark for evaluating persistent
  compromise in autonomous AI agents, including memory poisoning, context
  drift, toolchain confusion, and delayed activation behaviors relevant to
  agent security and frontier model safety evaluation.
